I just wrote a few words to the NetHack wiki, discussing the shopkeeper
names, and I noticed that four shopkeeper names had disappeared from the
code.

The list of bookstore keepers in Hack 1.0 (who then sold only scrolls, as
spellbooks were still yet to be) is:

char *shkbooks[] = {
	/* Eire */
	"Skibbereen", "Kanturk", "Rath Luirc", "Ennistymon", "Lahinch",
	"Loughrea", "Croagh", "Maumakeogh", "Ballyjamesduff",
	"Kinnegad", "Lugnaquillia", "Enniscorthy", "Gweebarra",
	"Kittamagh", "Nenagh", "Sneem", "Ballingeary", "Kilgarvan",
	"Cahersiveen", "Glenbeigh", "Kilmihil", "Kiltamagh",
	"Droichead Atha", "Inniscrone", "Clonegal", "Lisnaskea",
	"Culdaff", "Dunfanaghy", "Inishbofin", "Kesh",
	0
};

But in NetHack 2.2a, four of those names mysteriously vanished,
specifically Loughrea, Croagh, Maumakeogh and Ballyjamesduff.  They
remain missing to this day.

An accidental deletion many years ago?  Or maybe "Ballyjamesduff" doesn't
seem Irish enough?


